== Related item ==

* Shinkaisan {{ill|10=ja|11=上宮寺 (佐久市)|Joguji Temple|en}} – Moved from this location to 2553 {{ill|10=ja|11=南佐久郡|Minamisaku District, Nagano|en}} Harajuku, Saku City ( {{ill|10=ja|11=田口村_(長野県)|Taguchi Village|en}}, {{ill|10=ja|11=田口青沼村|Taguchi Aonuma Village|en}}, {{ill|10=ja|11=臼田町|Usuda, Nagano|en}}, {{ill|10=ja|11=田口村_(長野県)|Minamisaku|en|4=fr|5=District de Minamisaku}} {{ill|10=ja|11=田口村_(長野県)|District|en}} ). The 12th temple {{ill|10=ja|11=佐久三十三観音|of the Saku Thirty-three Kannon Temples|en}} . Founded by Prince Kamimiya in 849 .
* Tairyozan {{ill|10=ja|11=蕃松院|Banshoin|en}} – Shitamachi 2893. An ancient Soto Zen temple. Built by {{ill|10=ja|11=依田康国|Yasukuni Yoda|en}} {{ill|10=ja|11=依田信蕃|as the memorial temple for Nobutaka|en}} Yoda <ref>{{Cite web|title=曹洞禅ナビ|url=http://sotozen-navi.com/|access-date=2024-03-01|website=曹洞禅ナビ}}</ref> <ref>{{Cite web|title=蕃松院 {{!}} 佐久市ホームページ|url=https://www.city.saku.nagano.jp/kanko/townguide/temp/bansyouin.html|access-date=2024-03-01|website=www.city.saku.nagano.jp}}</ref> <ref>{{Cite web|title=蕃松院|url=http://www.zephyr.dti.ne.jp/bushi/siseki/bansyouin.htm|access-date=2024-03-01|website=www.zephyr.dti.ne.jp}}</ref>
* {{ill|10=ja|11=能満寺 (佐久市)|Nomanji Temple|en}} – There is a monument to the founder of the temple, {{ill|10=ja|11=割元|Kobayashi|en}} Magozaemon Kiyomori.
* {{ill|10=ja|11=龍岡城|Tatsuoka Castle|en}} – {{ill|10=ja|11=田口村_(長野県)|Okutono Village|en}} {{ill|10=ja|11=奥殿藩|Okutono Domain|en|4=fr|5=Domaine d'Okutono}} Headquarters and Camp
* {{ill|10=ja|11=龍岡城駅|Tatsuokajō Station|en}}
